% f: (documentation Decibel EnglishLanguage "The decibel (symbol: dB) is a relative unit of measurement equal to one tenth of a bel (B). It expresses the ratio of two values of a power or root-power quantity on a logarithmic scale. Two signals whose levels differ by one decibel have a power ratio of 101/ 10 (approximately 1.26) or root-power ratio of 101⁄20 (approximately 1.12).[from Wikipedia]")
